From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:09:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(route): one-use subscription tickets for browser
 WebSockets

Problem: every WebSocket subscription (socket.io, /event/{source},
/action/{source}) skips authentication, because browsers cannot set an
Authorization header on a WebSocket and the dashboard sends none. Anyone
who reaches the dashboard's port can read every event.

Why not a token in the URL (?token=, as other CasaOS forks do): a
long-lived access token would land in access logs, proxy logs, browser
history and referers; the gateway already refuses URL tokens for that
reason.

This: POST /v2/message_bus/ticket, with the normal Authorization header,
answers 204 with a cookie holding a ticket that is
- random (256 bit), valid for one handshake and at most 30 s,
- bound to the user and the User-Agent,
- HttpOnly (scripts cannot read it), SameSite=Strict (never sent from
  another site, so no cross-site WebSocket hijacking), Path-scoped to
  /v2/message_bus/, Secure under HTTPS,
- capped at 64 pending.
The browser sends it with the WebSocket handshake by itself; the
handshake redeems it. Nothing reusable ever appears in a URL. This is
the pattern the root service already uses for its SSH terminal
(route/v1/ssh.go). Tickets open subscription handshakes only.

Compatible on its own: the unauthenticated WebSocket exemption stays
until the dashboard sends tickets (ReCasaOS-UI: "subscribe with a
ticket"), then a follow-up removes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 api/message_bus/openapi.yaml |  42 +++++++++++
 codegen/message_bus_api.go   | 142 +++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 route/routers.go             |   9 +++
 route/ticket.go              | 142 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 route/ticket_test.go         | 140 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 418 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 route/ticket.go
 create mode 100644 route/ticket_test.go

diff --git a/api/message_bus/openapi.yaml b/api/message_bus/openapi.yaml
index 15f66aa..2400574 100644
--- a/api/message_bus/openapi.yaml
+++ b/api/message_bus/openapi.yaml
@@ -294,6 +294,30 @@ paths:
           description: |
             The connection will be upgraded to a WebSocket connection and the client will receive actions as they are triggered.
 
+  /ticket:
+    post:
+      summary: Issue a subscription ticket
+      description: |
+        Browsers cannot set an `Authorization` header on a WebSocket, and tokens are never accepted
+        in URLs (they leak into logs, history and referers). A browser therefore asks for a ticket
+        first, with its normal `Authorization` header, and then opens the subscription.
+
+        The ticket is returned only as a cookie: random, valid for one subscription handshake and
+        at most 30 seconds, bound to the user and User-Agent, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`, and
+        scoped to this API's path, so the browser sends it with the WebSocket handshake and nowhere
+        else. The same pattern as the root service's SSH terminal login.
+      operationId: issueSubscriptionTicket
+      tags:
+        - SocketIO Endpoints
+        - Websocket Endpoints
+      responses:
+        "204":
+          description: Ticket issued in the `Set-Cookie` header.
+        "403":
+          $ref: "#/components/responses/ResponseForbidden"
+        "429":
+          $ref: "#/components/responses/ResponseTooManyRequests"
+
   /socket.io:
     get:
       summary: Subscribe to events and actions (SocketIO)
@@ -525,6 +549,24 @@ components:
           example:
             message: "Conflict"
 
+    ResponseForbidden:
+      description: Forbidden
+      content:
+        application/json:
+          schema:
+            $ref: "#/components/schemas/BaseResponse"
+          example:
+            message: "Forbidden"
+
+    ResponseTooManyRequests:
+      description: Too Many Requests
+      content:
+        application/json:
+          schema:
+            $ref: "#/components/schemas/BaseResponse"
+          example:
+            message: "Too Many Requests"
+
     GetEventTypesOK:
       description: OK
       content:
